t and so we want  kids to be grounded and have a lot to do  um and so we've put them to work whether  it's like  building the garden or you can hear all  the birds in the background myself i can  hear your rooster  dude my kids are on chicken duty um  we just i don't i have we have chickens  but i don't allow a rooster  i'm like oh gosh we've got such a bad  coyote and fox problem we need a boat oh  i got a field so i got you  killed that's awesome that you put your  kids to work that's the same thing that  my husband and i were doing we wanted  our kids to be able to actually because  i grew up in the countryside and so did  he  so is it true that you not only write  books over shoot a talk show  run a farm but you're also helping out  local hospitals  so many of our good friends here in the  hudson valley are  are members of the medical field you  know whether it's like doctors or nurses  or emts  and so the immediacy of helping all of  them was really important so we started  sewing masks right away  encouraging other people to sew masks we  um a lot of the moms  soccer moms we all got together and  started raising  money to feed all the medical workers at  our coveted testing facility  so now that same group of people we're  taking all that energy we had for the  pandemic  and we're putting it towards our school  teachers now because we have no idea  what school is going to look like in the  fall and our teachers can't afford  crayons  and paper and books and stuff for the  kids let alone  ppe for everybody to make it safe so  we're trying to  even thinking about like a lot of us  with kids  our kids they might still be home and a  lot of parents don't have access to all  those supplies  like a lot of you know so not every kid  has a computer or an  ipad um but your new book is about  your life up there and i think that it's  really cool so what  what inspired you to do is it because  basically you had that other lifestyle  and you wanted it slowed down a bit  l