ah you're like there's not a that's it  was me and my my sister and her family  and i was like uh there's not  people don't work here just us holding  it down  so so i mean this is so i would just  want to say  hi everybody okay obviously jeffrey dean  morgan has um  involved he's now involved in the  interview and i'm such a big fan i love  the walking dead so i'm just going to  say that shout out  um so thank you thank you for hanging  out with us but um  so hillary told us how special your  community is up there um what's your  favorite part about it she told us why  she kind of liked  living up there and out of the the  limelight i love it as well obviously we  have a place in  montana um but i want to know why you  like that kind of life and but also i  heard you owned a candy shop do you  still own a candy shop  yeah we do i i mean i think just getting  out of los  angeles for us was such it was so needed  i think just for our well-being  um and then having kids and it started  out with  obviously just the one gus and we  thought that this kind of lifestyle  uh was very conducive to raising a good  kid  uh and so far so good uh he's good for  now  he's alive he's breathing yeah yeah  he's pretty good and you know george is  a real uh animal whisperer too  it turns out so she her and i are the we  love our animals  gus and i are the gardeners they're the  animal people yeah she spends a lot of  time in the  chicken coops um she loves the chickens  for whatever she loves all the animals  but she loves the chickens like every  night it's a thing she has to be  has to have her chicken duck time that's  so cool too to have both worlds thank  you guys so much  for hanging out with us i love your  beautiful farm thank you for having us  um y'all be sure to pick up hillary's  new book the rural  diaries rural is hard for me to say  subscribe to my channel subscribe to my  channel  subscribe to my channel subscribe to my  channel please don't make me keep going

